You are enriching a semantic model for a SQL data agent. The dataset schemas below are already structurally defined (tables, columns, keys, relationships, metrics are authoritative). Your ONLY job is to add business language — aliases and one-line meanings.

Produce ONE YAML document with a single top-level section `annotations` (strict YAML, no markdown fences, no commentary):

annotations:
  - table: <table>
    field_notes:
      - name: <column>
        synonyms: [<alias1>, <alias2>]
        description: <one-line business meaning in English>

Rules:
- Only add synonyms and descriptions to EXISTING columns. NEVER add, rename, delete columns, tables, expressions, keys, or relationships; NEVER change datatypes; NEVER invent metrics or aggregate SQL.
- Synonyms are the natural-language words a user would say for this column ("region", "area" for column A3). At most 3 short lowercase phrases.
- For opaque column names (A1..A16 style) give the probable business meaning from your domain knowledge; empty synonyms [] only when you genuinely cannot tell.
- description: one short line, plain language.
- Cover every column in the chunk; skip none.

annotations:
  - table: <table>
    field_notes:
      - name: <column>
        synonyms: []
        description: ""